@startuml
title Sekwencja: zapis stanu symulacji i wczytanie przy starcie
' Przypadki użycia: "Zapisać stan symulacji", "Wczytać stan symulacji"
' Wejście/wyjście: ObjectOutputStream / ObjectInputStream (serializacja grafu obiektów).

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor "Operator" as Operator
participant "main : Main" as Main
participant "controller : SimulationController" as Controller
participant "command : SaveCommand" as Command
participant "storage : SimulationStorage" as Storage
participant "simulation : Simulation" as Simulation
participant "view : SimulationView" as View
participant "runner : SimulationRunner" as Runner

== Zapis (wątek konsoli) ==

Operator -> Controller : processInput("save stan.dat")
activate Controller
Controller -> Command : execute(controller)
activate Command
Command -> Storage : save(simulation, path)
activate Storage
Storage -> Storage : new ObjectOutputStream(new FileOutputStream(path))
Storage -> Simulation : synchronized(simulation) { writeObject(simulation) }
note right of Simulation : zapisywany jest cały graf obiektów\n(Lock, Gate, Chamber, kolejki, statki, Statistics);\nlisteners w Lock są transient
Storage --> Command : ok
deactivate Storage
Command --> Controller : "Zapisano stan do stan.dat"
deactivate Command
Controller -> View : showMessage(text)
deactivate Controller

== Wczytanie przy starcie programu ==

Operator -> Main : uruchomienie z argumentem stan.dat
activate Main
Main -> Storage : load(path)
activate Storage
Storage -> Storage : new ObjectInputStream(new FileInputStream(path))
Storage -> Simulation ** : readObject()
Simulation -> Simulation : readObject(): ponownie zarejestruj Statistics jako listener
Storage --> Main : simulation
deactivate Storage

Main -> Controller ** : new SimulationController(simulation, view)
Controller -> Simulation : addListener(view)
Main -> Controller : start()
Controller -> Runner ** : new SimulationRunner(simulation, view, tickMillis)
Controller -> Runner : new Thread(runner).start()
deactivate Main

note over Storage
  Błędy I/O (IOException, ClassNotFoundException) są łapane w kontrolerze
  i pokazywane widokowi jako komunikat – symulacja działa dalej.
end note

@enduml
